{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe CLI read handlers `_cmd_list` and `_cmd_session_logs` (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py`)\ngate initialization on a bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)` and call `_engine_support/reads.py` state\nfunctions (`list_states` / `recent_session_logs_state` → `reduce_all_tickets`) **directly**,\nbypassing the hardened read chokepoint `_reads._tracker` that `rapt-dreadable-dromedary`\n(`aefe-614a-2631-4117`) switched to `store_is_usable`. A tracker directory that EXISTS but is not a\nusable store (no `.git`, or `.git` with an unresolvable HEAD mid-clone) satisfies `isdir`, so these\npaths print `[]` at exit 0 for a broken/mid-clone store instead of rejecting it — the exact\nfallback-masking rapt-d removed from the library, surviving on the CLI surface.\n\n## Root cause & attribution (see RCA comment)\n\nUnmet-obligation / missed-consumer-update: rapt-d hardened the library/MCP read chokepoint +\nwrite gate and created the \"reads reject a present-but-unusable store via `store_is_usable`\"\nobligation; the CLI consumers were never updated. `caused_by = aefe-614a-2631-4117`, close-class\n`regression` (parity/consistency regression introduced by rapt-d's asymmetric hardening). Date test:\nthe isdir lines predate rapt-d (2026-06-24 vs 2026-08-29), so they are the correct-at-the-time\nconsumer, not the origin.\n\n## Fix (faithful parity — reuse the authority predicate, invent nothing)\n\nReplace the bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)` reject gate at `reads_cli.py:340` (`_cmd_list`) and\n`:384` (`_cmd_session_logs`) with `rebar._store.store_usability.store_is_usable(tracker)` — the same\nstdlib-only predicate the parent fix made the read/write source of truth. This is a zero-contract-\nchange extension: an ABSENT store still rejects (rc 1, unchanged), a valid EMPTY store still returns\n`[]` rc 0 (unchanged), and only the present-but-unusable case flips from `[]` rc 0 → rc 1\n\"not initialized\", matching the library.\n\n## Parity census (Step 7, Axis 2) — full channel disposition\n\n- **`_cmd_list` (`reads_cli.py:340`)** — FIX (observable rc 0→1 for broken/mid-clone).\n- **`_cmd_session_logs` (`reads_cli.py:384`)** — FIX (observable rc 0→1).\n- **`descendants.py:25`** — N/A: deliberately tolerant read (`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_envelope.py:17`), consumed by `close_precheck` + `llm/overlap`; swap provably unobservable; rejecting would alter intended tolerant behavior.\n- **`next_batch.py:154`** — N/A: not a readiness gate (guards `os.scandir` for tombstones, reached only after epic resolution); broken store already fails closed rc 1 (`EpicNotFound`, runtime-proven).\n- **`repo_snapshot.py:619`** — N/A: SHA-pinning helper with its own stronger `git rev-parse --git-dir` probe after the isdir.\n- **`_engine_support/reads.py:251`** — N/A: best-effort background-sync guard, not a readiness/init gate.\n- **MCP / library channel** — OK: funnels through `_reads._tracker` → `store_is_usable` (rapt-d).\n- **CLI `search`/`ready`** — separate finding (no gate at all; also masks absent), filed as `97e9-e663-a94e-4038` (`discovered_from`).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `_cmd_list` (`reads_cli.py:340`) gates on `store_is_usable`: a present-but-unusable store\n      (no `.git`) reports rc 1 \"not initialized\", not `[]` rc 0.\n- [ ] `_cmd_session_logs` (`reads_cli.py:384`) gates on `store_is_usable`: same for a\n      present-but-unusable store.\n- [ ] Both reject a mid-clone store (`.git` present, HEAD unresolvable) with rc 1.\n- [ ] An existing, empty, INITIALIZED store still returns `[]` rc 0 for both (contract preserved,\n      anchored so a vacuous empty cannot pass) — and an ABSENT store still rc 1 (unchanged).\n- [ ] Regression per site: reverting either gate to bare `os.path.isdir` returns the\n      broken/mid-clone case to RED (defect-seeded mutation guard).\n- [ ] Structural class guard: a test asserts no CLI reject-gate in `reads_cli.py` uses bare\n      `os.path.isdir(tracker)` for the readiness decision (fails if a new instance appears)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788065550406579361,"uuid":"70e84bc7-ff66-425e-ac67-3a9efa4f78eb"}